# 📒 Progress Log — May 26–27, 2025

---

## **May 26 — GitHub Branch Troubles & VS Code**

* Spent 2–3 hours digging into GitHub branch problems and syncing with Visual Studio Code.
* Faced some weird errors: couldn’t sync the changes to the right branch, had issues with the default branch, and got stuck on unknown conflicts.
* Tried to document every bug and mistake in GitHub Issues (wrote short summaries for each).
* In the end, decided to start from scratch: created a new working folder, opened it in VS Code, pulled the branch again — and suddenly everything just worked.
* Lesson: Sometimes, it’s faster to “nuke and pave” your environment than to try fixing broken sync configs.

---

## **May 27 — Linux Services, Scripts & Troubleshooting**

* Went deep into **systemd services** on Linux.
* Wrote 4 new bash scripts and wrapped them as systemd services (both always-on and scheduled types).
* Broke things on purpose: messed up unit files, watched logs via `systemctl status`, fixed timing/dependency issues for fun.
* Figured out how to automate service restarts and fix classic errors (`start-limit-hit`, wrong paths, bad permissions, etc.).
* Started keeping a running “gotchas” list for the most common systemd errors (see GitHub Issues).

---


## **May 28–29 — Busy Days & Quick Reviews**

* Lots of work, barely any time to study.
* Spent about 1.5 hours each day reviewing previous materials.
* No new topics, just refreshing what’s already covered.
